work de dados de prova de Rust","framework de dados de prova de Rust alternative","Rust vs outros frameworks","instalar o framework de dados de prova de Rust","guia de configuração do framework de dados de prova de Rust","desenvolvimento de aplicativos com Rust","segurança de aplicativos com Rust"],"ru":["как использовать фреймворк носимых данных языка Rust","что такое фреймворк носимых данных языка Rust","фреймворк носимых данных языка Rust альтернатива","Rust vs другие фреймворки","установка фреймворка носимых данных языка Rust","руководство по настройке фреймворка носимых данных языка Rust","разработка приложений с помощью Rust","безопасность приложений с помощью Rust"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام إطار بيانات لغة روست","ما هو إطار بيانات لغة روست","إطار بيانات لغة روست بديل","روست مقابل إطارات أخرى","تثبيت إطار بيانات لغة روست","دليل إعداد إطار بيانات لغة روست","تطوير التطبيقات بلغة روست","أمان التطبيقات بلغة روست"]}},"owner":"tachyon-zcash","repo":"ragu","repoPath":"tachyon-zcash/ragu","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-04T13:07:01.682Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"book-review","description":"Review any part of the book using parallel specialist agents","bodyPreview":"# Book Review\n\nReview part of the book specified by `$ARGUMENTS`, using the project''s book\nreview policies.\n\n## Step 1: Figure Out What to Review\n\nThe user''s `$ARGUMENTS` could be anything. Interpret them:\n\n| Arguments | What to do |\n|-----------|-----------|\n| *(empty)* | Run `git diff -- book/src/` and `git diff --cached -- book/src/`. Review the uncommitted changes. If no changes, say so and stop. |\n| A file path | Read that file. Review the whole chapter. |\n| A file path with lines (`foo.md:","body":"# Book Review\n\nReview part of the book specified by `$ARGUMENTS`, using the project''s book\nreview policies.\n\n## Step 1: Figure Out What to Review\n\nThe user''s `$ARGUMENTS` could be anything. Interpret them:\n\n| Arguments | What to do |\n|-----------|-----------|\n| *(empty)* | Run `git diff -- book/src/` and `git diff --cached -- book/src/`. Review the uncommitted changes. If no changes, say so and stop. |\n| A file path | Read that file. Review the whole chapter. |\n| A file path with lines (`foo.md:50-80`) | Read that file. Focus the review on those lines (but read the full file for context). |\n| Multiple file paths | Read all of them. Review each, and also look for consistency across them. |\n| A section heading or topic name | Use Grep/Glob to find where that topic is discussed in `book/src/`. Read those sections. Review them. |\n| A conceptual description (\"how we explain X\", \"the transition between Y and Z\") | Search the book to find the relevant passages. Read them with surrounding context. Review them as a unit. |\n| A mix of the above | Handle each part, then review the union. |\n\nIf you''re unsure what the user means, ask before launching reviewers.\n\n## Step 2: Discover and Launch Reviewers\n\n1. Use Glob to find all `.claude/book-review/*.md` files.\n2. Read `.claude/book-review/standards.md` (master standards shared by all\n   reviewers).\n3. For EACH policy file **except `standards.md`**, launch a `general-purpose`\n   Task agent (use model `sonnet`). Give each agent a prompt constructed from\n   this template — adapt it based on what you''re reviewing:\n\n   > You are reviewing part of \"The Ragu Book,\" a technical book about a\n   > recursive proof system (proof-carrying data framework).\n   >\n   > Read these files:\n   > - `.claude/book-review/standards.md` (master standards that always apply)\n   > - `.claude/book-review/{focus}.md` (your specific review policy)\n   >\n   > **What to review:** {describe the specific content — file paths, line\n   > ranges, the topic, whatever the user specified. If reviewing a diff,\n   > include the diff text and list the full file paths for context.}\n   >\n   > {If the scope is a diff or a narrow range, add: \"Focus on the specified\n   > content. Flag issues in surrounding text ONLY if the specified content\n   > introduced an inconsistency with it.\"}\n   >\n   > {If the scope spans multiple files or a concept, add: \"Pay attention to\n   > consistency across the passages. Flag contradictions, redundancies, or\n   > gaps in the explanation as it spans these locations.\"}\n   >\n   > If the policy references other files (like `book/macros.txt` or\n   > `book/src/appendix/terminology.md`), read those too.\n   >\n   > For each finding:\n   > - **Location**: file path and quoted text (or line number)\n   > - **Issue**: what''s wrong, specifically\n   > - **Suggestion**: a concrete rewrite, not just \"improve this\"\n   > - **Severity**: `must-fix` (clearly wrong/confusing) or `suggestion`\n   >\n   > Stay within your policy''s scope. Be specific. If you find no real issues,\n   > say so — don''t manufacture problems.\n\n   Additionally, read `book/FIXME.md` and extract the `###`-level headings\n   under `## Deferred Issues`. Include them in each reviewer''s prompt as a\n   bullet list with the instruction:\n   > The following issues are already tracked and deferred. Do NOT raise\n   > findings that duplicate or overlap with these items. If your finding\n   > is essentially the same issue, omit it.\n   >\n   > {bullet list of ### headings from book/FIXME.md}\n   >\n   > However, if while reviewing you notice that a deferred issue appears to\n   > have been **resolved** by existing content or is now easily resolvable\n   > given changes in the surrounding text, mention it as a separate\n   > observation (not a finding). Format:\n   > - **Resolvable FIXME**: \"{FIXME heading}\" — {brief explanation of why\n   >   it appears resolved or how to resolve it now}\n\n   Launch ALL agents in parallel (multiple Task calls in one message).\n\n## Step 3: Run Automated Link Checks\n\nIn parallel with the reviewer agents (launched in Step 2), run the automated\nQA scripts to detect broken links and dead pages:\n\n1. Run `python3 qa/book/broken_links.py` — finds broken internal links and\n   invalid anchors (requires `mdbook` to be installed).\n2. Run `python3 qa/book/dead_pages.py` — finds markdown files not listed in\n   `SUMMARY.md`.\n3. Run `python3 qa/book/line_width.py` — finds lines exceeding the\n   80-character width limit (excludes code blocks, math blocks, and other\n   exempt content).\n\nIf either script fails to run (e.g., `mdbook` is not installed), note the\nfailure in your output but do not block the review. Include any findings from\nthese scripts alongside the reviewer agents'' results in the synthesis step.\n\n## Step 4: Synthesize\n\nOnce all agents return, organize findings by location (earliest in the book\nfirst). If multiple reviewers flagged overlapping concerns, merge them. Present:\n\n- **Must-fix** issues first\n- **Suggestions** second\n- For each finding, note which reviewer(s) identified it\n\nIf the review scope was cross-file or conceptual, add a short section at the end\nabout cross-cutting observations (consistency, narrative coherence, etc.).\n\nBefore presenting findings, read `book/FIXME.md` and remove any finding that\nsubstantially overlaps with an already-deferred issue (match against the `###`\nheadings). If you remove findings this way, do not mention them at all.\n\nIf any reviewer flagged a resolvable FIXME, collect them in a **Potentially\nResolvable FIXMEs** section after the main findings. The user can then use\n`/book-fixme` to address them.\n\n## Step 5: Validate Proposed Changes\n\nAfter synthesizing findings, but before presenting them to the user:\n\n1. Collect all proposed changes (the \"suggestion\" field from each finding) into\n   a single numbered list — the **proposed plan**.\n2. For EACH policy file (same set as Step 2 — every `.claude/book-review/*.md`\n   except `standards.md`), launch a `general-purpose` Task agent (model\n   `sonnet`) with this prompt:\n\n   > You are validating a set of proposed book edits against review policies.\n   >\n   > Read these files:\n   > - `.claude/book-review/standards.md` (master standards)\n   > - `.claude/book-review/{focus}.md` (your policy)\n   >\n   > Here is the proposed plan of changes:\n   > {numbered list of proposed changes with locations and suggested rewrites}\n   >\n   > For each proposed change, check whether applying it would **introduce** a\n   > violation of any rule in your policy or the master standards. Only flag\n   > real conflicts — do not restate rules that are already satisfied.\n   >\n   > For each conflict found:\n   > - **Change #**: which proposed change\n   > - **Rule violated**: quote the relevant policy text\n   > - **Conflict**: explain specifically how the suggestion violates the rule\n   > - **Resolution**: suggest how to fix the suggestion to comply\n   >\n   > If no proposed changes conflict with your policy, say so.\n\n   Launch ALL agents in parallel.\n\n3. Merge validation feedback into the findings. For each conflict:\n   - If the validator provides a compliant alternative, replace the original\n     suggestion with the corrected version.\n   - If the conflict has no clear resolution, annotate the finding with the\n     conflict so the user can decide during triage.\n\n4. If any suggestions were corrected, briefly note it in the synthesis output\n   (e.g., \"Grammar validator caught that suggestion #3 would violate the\n   lowercase-technical-terms rule; corrected.\").\n\n## Step 6: Triage\n\nAfter presenting findings, use AskUserQuestion to let the user decide the\ndisposition of each finding (or group of closely related findings). For each,\noffer:\n\n- **Fix** — apply the suggested fix now\n- **Skip** — drop this finding; do not record it anywhere\n- **Defer** — record this finding in `book/FIXME.md` for future attention\n\nIf there are many findings, you may batch them into logical groups and ask\nabout each group rather than each individual finding.\n\n## Step 7: Apply Fixes\n\nFor each finding the user chose to **fix**:\n\n1. Read the target file to get the current content.\n2. Apply the suggested change using the Edit tool. If the finding is a group\n   (e.g., \"add slugs to these 15 headings\"), apply all changes in the group.\n3. After applying all fixes, run any relevant QA scripts to verify the changes\n   don''t introduce new issues:\n   - If formatting changes were made: `python3 qa/book/line_width.py`\n   - If links or headings were changed: `python3 qa/book/broken_links.py`\n4. Briefly report what was changed and any QA results.\n\n## Step 8: Record Deferred Issues\n\nFor each finding the user chose to **defer**:\n\n1. Read `book/FIXME.md`.\n2. Check whether a substantially similar issue is already listed. First scan\n   the `###` headings for a potential match; if a heading looks similar, read\n   the paragraph beneath it to confirm it describes the same issue. Only skip\n   if both the heading and description match — do not treat a heading match\n   alone as a duplicate.\n3. If the issue is new, append it as a new `###`-level subsection under\n   `## Deferred Issues`, following the existing format: a short descriptive\n   heading, then a concise paragraph explaining the issue and its location.\n4. Write the updated file.\n\nAfter recording, confirm what was deferred and remind the user they can use\n`/book-refine` to turn feedback into policy improvements.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-04T13:24:38.796Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Language Agents like Claude Code or AutoGPT needing advanced text analysis capabilities for reviewing book content.","zh":"适合于 Claude Code 或 AutoGPT 等语言代理，需要高级文本分析功能来审阅书籍内容。","ja":"Claude Code や AutoGPT などの言語エージェントに適しており、書籍コンテンツのレビューに高度なテキスト分析機能が必要です。","ko":"Claude Code 또는 AutoGPT 같은 언어 에이전트에 적합하며, 책 내용을 검토하기 위해 고급 텍스트 분석 기능이 필요합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de lenguaje como Claude Code o AutoGPT que necesitan capacidades de análisis de texto avanzadas para revisar contenido de libros.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de langage comme Claude Code ou AutoGPT nécessitant des capacités d''analyse de texte avancées pour examiner le contenu de livres.","de":"Ideal für Sprachagenten wie Claude Code oder AutoGPT, die erweiterte Textanalysefunktionen zur Überprüfung von Buchinhalten benötigen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Linguagem como Claude Code ou AutoGPT que precisam de capacidades avançadas de análise de texto para revisar conteúdo de livros.","ru":"Идеально подходит для языковых агентов, таких как Claude Code или AutoGPT, которые требуют расширенных возможностей анализа текста для просмотра содержания книг.","ar":"مثالي لعميل لغة مثل Claude Code أو AutoGPT الذي يحتاج إلى قدرات分析 متقدمة للنص لمراجعة محتوى الكتب."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to interpret and review book chapters using Git diff analysis, supporting review of uncommitted changes, specific file paths, and line ranges within files like ''foo.md:10-20'', utilizing Rust language proof-carrying data frameworks.","zh":"赋予代理审阅书籍章节的能力，使用 Git diff 分析，支持审阅未提交的更改、特定文件路径以及文件中的行范围，例如 ''foo.md:10-20''，利用 Rust 语言证明携带数据框架。","ja":"エージェントが書籍の章を解釈してレビューできるようにし、Git diff 分析を使用して、コミットされていない変更、特定のファイルパス、ファイル内の行範囲（例：''foo.md:10-20''）のレビューをサポートし、Rust 言語の証明付きデータフレームワークを利用します。","ko":"에이전트가 책 章을 해석하고 검토할 수 있도록 하며, Git diff 분석을 사용하여 커밋되지 않은 변경 사항, 특정 파일 경로 및 파일 내의 줄 범위(''foo.md:10-20'' 예시)를 검토하도록 지원하며, Rust 언어 증명 携带 데이터 프레임워크를 활용합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a interpretar y revisar capítulos de libros utilizando el análisis de Git diff, lo que admite la revisión de cambios no confirmados, rutas de archivo específicas y rangos de líneas dentro de archivos como ''foo.md:10-20'', utilizando frameworks de datos de prueba de lenguaje Rust.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''interpréter et d''examiner des chapitres de livres en utilisant l''analyse de Git diff, ce qui prend en charge l''examen des modifications non validées, des chemins de fichiers spécifiques et des plages de lignes à l''intérieur de fichiers comme ''foo.md:10-20'', en utilisant des frameworks de données de preuve de langage Rust.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, Kapitel von Büchern mithilfe der Git-Diff-Analyse zu interpretieren und zu überprüfen, was die Überprüfung von nicht committeten Änderungen, spezifischer Dateipfade und Zeilenbereiche innerhalb von Dateien wie ''foo.md:10-20'' unterstützt, unter Verwendung von Rust-Sprachnachweisdatenframeworks.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a interpretar e revisar capítulos de livros usando análise Git diff, suportando revisão de alterações não comprometidas, caminhos de arquivo específicos e intervalos de linhas dentro de arquivos como ''foo.md:10-20'', utilizando frameworks de dados de prova de linguagem Rust.","ru":"Позволяет агентам интерпретировать и просматривать главы книг, используя анализ Git diff, поддерживая просмотр незафиксированных изменений, определенные пути файлов и диапазоны строк внутри файлов, таких как ''foo.md:10-20'', используя фреймворки языка Rust для переноса данных.","ar":"يُمكّن الوكيل من تفسير ومراجعة فصول الكتب باستخدام تحليل Git diff، مع دعم مراجعة التغييرات غير الملتزمة، مسارات الملفات المحددة، ونطاقات السطور داخل الملفات مثل ''foo.md:10-20''، باستخدام إطار العمل للغة روست لحمل البيانات."},"useCases":{"en":["Reviewing uncommitted book chapter changes","Analyzing specific file paths within a book project","Debugging line ranges in markdown files"],"zh":["审阅未提交的书籍章节更改","分析书籍项目中的特定文件路径","调试标记文件中的行范围"],"ja":["コミットされていない書籍章の変更のレビュー","書籍プロジェクト内の特定のファイルパスの分析","マークダウンファイル内の行範囲のデバッグ"],"ko":["커밋되지 않은 책 章 변경 사항 검토","책 프로젝트 내 특정 파일 경로 분석","마크다운 파일 내 줄 범위 디버깅"],"es":["Revisar cambios no confirmados de capítulos de libros","Analizar rutas de archivo específicas dentro de un proyecto de libro","Depurar rangos de líneas en archivos markdown"],"fr":["Examiner les modifications non validées des chapitres de livres","Analyser des chemins de fichiers spécifiques à l''intérieur d''un projet de livre","Déboguer des plages de lignes dans des fichiers markdown"],"de":["Überprüfen von nicht committeten Änderungen an Buchkapiteln","Analysieren von spezifischen Dateipfaden innerhalb eines Buchprojekts","Fehlerbehebung von Zeilenbereichen in Markdown-Dateien"],"pt":["Revisar alterações não comprometidas de capítulos de livros","Analizar caminhos de arquivo específicos dentro de um projeto de livro","Depurar intervalos de linhas em arquivos markdown"],"ru":["Просмотр незафиксированных изменений глав книг","Анализ определенных путей файлов внутри проекта книги","Отладка диапазонов строк в файлах markdown"],"ar":["مراجعة التغييرات غير الملتزمة لفصول الكتب","تحليل مسارات الملفات المحددة داخل مشروع كتاب","تصحيح أخطاء نطاقات السطور في ملفات ماركداون"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Git installation and configuration","Limited to reviewing content in ''book/src/'' directory","Needs Rust language proof-carrying data framework compatibility"],"zh":["需要 Git 安装和配置","仅限于 ''book/src/'' 目录内的内容审阅","需要 Rust 语言证明携带数据框架兼容性"],"ja":["Git のインストールと設定が必要","''book/src/'' ディレクトリ内のコンテンツのレビューのみ","Rust 言語の証明付きデータフレームワークとの互換性が必要"],"ko":["Git 설치 및 구성이 필요","''book/src/'' 디렉토리 내의 내용 검토만 가능","Rust 언어 증명携带 데이터 프레임워크와의 호환성이 필요"],"es":["Requiere instalación y configuración de Git","Limitado a la revisión de contenido en el directorio ''book/src/''","Necesita compatibilidad con el framework de datos de prueba de lenguaje Rust"],"fr":["Nécessite l''installation et la configuration de Git","Limité à l''examen du contenu dans le répertoire ''book/src/''","Nécessite la compatibilité avec le framework de données de preuve de langage Rust"],"de":["Benötigt Git-Installation und -Konfiguration","Begrenzt auf die Überprüfung von Inhalten im Verzeichnis ''book/src/''","Benötigt Kompatibilität mit dem Rust-Sprachnachweisdatenframework"],"pt":["Requer instalação e configuração do Git","Limitado à revisão de conteúdo no diretório ''book/src/''","Necessita de compatibilidade com framework de dados de prova de linguagem Rust"],"ru":["Требует установки и настройки Git","Ограничен просмотром содержания в директории ''book/src/''","Требует совместимости с фреймворком языка Rust для переноса данных"],"ar":["يتطلب تثبيت وتكوين Git","محدود بمراجعة المحتوى في الدليل ''book/src/''","يحتاج إلى توافق مع إطار العمل للغة روست لحمل البيانات"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"03ecd3daf1c141683fc43f208d3e2aa567dcb6a2478d219704e3e6dbd58cc56e","qualityScore":24}');
